# Valve's arm64 Steam Runtime (steamrt3c), the container Valve's arm64 Steam client runs in.
#
# Read by /usr/lib/retroforge/steam-bootstrap, which downloads it into the player's home on the first
# `steam` (~/.local/share/retroforge/steam-runtime/<version>/), checks the sha256, and gives
# /usr/bin/steam its `run`. The client needs it: it loads steamui.so, which needs GTK2 and the rest of
# the runtime. The client strips LD_LIBRARY_PATH, so it has to run inside the container
# (docs/steam-arm64.md).
#
# Not in the image: it unpacks to 222 MB, and a root slot is 2 GB (image/partition-table.txt).
# It is also not in the client's own update manifest: that manifest's runtime_steamrt_linuxarm64 is the
# x86_64/i386 runtime for FEX games, not this one.
#
# Same fields as a packages/*/prebuilt.pin. The URL is Valve's versioned image directory, not the
# latest-steam-client-general-availability alias, so the bytes cannot move under the sha256. The
# sha256 is from that directory's SHA256SUMS, and a download was checked against it on 2026-10-15
# (layout: steam-runtime-steamrt-arm64/{run,_v2-entry-point,pressure-vessel/,steamrt3c_platform_*/}).
#
# TO BUMP: read repo.steampowered.com/steamrt3c/images/latest-steam-client-general-availability.txt,
# then set version + url + sha256 together from that directory's SHA256SUMS. A player's old version
# is removed once the new one is in place. Valve prunes old directories (the oldest left on
# 2026-10-15 was 3c.0.20260526), so a fresh card fails to set Steam up once this one goes. Bump it
# before that happens.
name: steam-runtime-steamrt-arm64
version: 3c.0.20260824.257593
url: https://repo.steampowered.com/steamrt3c/images/3c.0.20260824.257593/steam-runtime-steamrt-arm64.tar.xz
sha256: 2f2be461b6a4360828e200e1644e18cd957eedc36a38e5a1e13a39276320b6e2
